+Triton ternary backend (skeleton)
+
+This folder contains guidance and minimal stubs for implementing a custom Triton backend
+or ONNXRuntime custom op that can perform efficient ternary arithmetic (bitpacked ternary).
+
+Paths:
+- ternary_backend_backend.cc   : C++ Triton backend skeleton (operator must implement)
+- build/                       : Build instructions for the backend (Dockerfile, Makefile)
+- tests/                       : unit tests for custom kernel
+
+Notes:
+- Implementing a performant ternary backend requires C++ kernels that decode bitpacked ternary
+  and perform low-precision arithmetic. For initial rollout you can:
+  1) Implement an ONNX custom op that unpacks ternary into float/FP16 and calls existing GEMM.
+  2) Or implement full ternary GEMM to reduce compute and memory bandwidth.
+- The following files provide minimal entry points and placeholders.
+
+See also:
+- Triton backend API docs: https://github.com/triton-inference-server/backend
+- ONNX custom ops: https://onnxruntime.ai/docs/how-to/add-custom-op
